WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.997
A Spark application has a driver and executors The
driver coordinates

00:00:06.023 --> 00:00:11.763
the application and builds the plan Executors run
tasks on data partitions

00:00:13.503 --> 00:00:17.661
A beginner-friendly way to think about this is that
the driver organizes the work and

00:00:17.687 --> 00:00:23.376
the executors perform the work We should avoid
collecting huge data back

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:26.153
to the driver because that can create memory
problems
